problem:
Problem description
- A single-period production and export planning problem is considered for a set $$\mathcal{I}$$ of commodities, where each commodity may be both a final export item and an intermediate input to other commodities.
- The planner is given a world-market export price $$\pi_i$$ for each commodity $$i \in \mathcal{I}$$, an imported-input expenditure coefficient $$\mu_i$$ per unit of commodity $$i$$, a technical input matrix $$A = [a_{ij}]$$, a labor requirement coefficient $$\lambda_i$$ per unit of commodity $$i$$, and optional commodity-specific production caps $$\bar{x}_i$$.
- The planning horizon is a single period $$\mathcal{T}$$, and the total available labor over $$\mathcal{T}$$ is $$L$$.
- The planning goal is to choose nonnegative production levels so that the total export value is maximized while imported-input expenditure is minimized, subject to all feasibility limits.
- The plan must respect the production recipe of each commodity, meaning that all required intermediate commodity inputs, imported inputs, and labor must be available for the chosen production level.
- Production may not exceed any commodity-specific capacity limit that is provided.
- Total labor used across all commodities must not exceed the available labor budget.
- All produced quantities are assumed to be sold or exported within the same planning period, with no inventory carryover, backlog, or explicit domestic demand cap unless a demand limit $$d_i$$ is provided as input.
- A solution is represented by:
  - $$x_i$$: the production and export quantity of commodity $$i \in \mathcal{I}$$.
  - $$z$$: the optimal value of the planning objective, representing the best net domestic value created by the plan.
  - $$m$$: the total imported-input expenditure implied by the chosen production plan.

Input Format
{
  "commodities": {
    "symbol": "$$\\mathcal{I}$$",
    "type": "array of identifiers",
    "description": "Set of commodities indexed by $$i \\in \\mathcal{I}$$."
  },
  "planning_horizon": {
    "symbol": "$$\\mathcal{T}$$",
    "type": "array or singleton set",
    "description": "Planning period set; in this problem, a single-period horizon."
  },
  "export_prices": {
    "symbol": "$$\\pi_i$$",
    "type": "array of length $$|\\mathcal{I}|$$",
    "description": "World-market export price per unit of commodity $$i$$."
  },
  "imported_input_expenditure": {
    "symbol": "$$\\mu_i$$",
    "type": "array of length $$|\\mathcal{I}|$$",
    "description": "Imported-input expenditure required per unit of commodity $$i$$."
  },
  "technical_input_coefficients": {
    "symbol": "$$A = [a_{ij}]$$",
    "type": "matrix of size $$|\\mathcal{I}| \\times |\\mathcal{I}|$$",
    "description": "For each produced commodity $$i$$, the amount of commodity $$j$$ needed per unit of $$i$$."
  },
  "labor_requirements": {
    "symbol": "$$\\lambda_i$$",
    "type": "array of length $$|\\mathcal{I}|$$",
    "description": "Labor required per unit of commodity $$i$$, expressed in a common labor unit."
  },
  "capacity_upper_bounds": {
    "symbol": "$$\\bar{x}_i$$",
    "type": "optional array of length $$|\\mathcal{I}|$$",
    "description": "Maximum allowable production for commodity $$i$$ when a cap exists; omitted or set to no upper bound otherwise."
  },
  "external_demand_cap": {
    "symbol": "$$d_i$$",
    "type": "optional array of length $$|\\mathcal{I}|$$",
    "description": "Optional external demand limit for commodity $$i$$; if absent, assume unlimited market absorption at price $$\\pi_i$$."
  },
  "total_labor_available": {
    "symbol": "$$L$$",
    "type": "scalar",
    "description": "Total labor available over $$\\mathcal{T}$$."
  },
  "objective_priority": {
    "symbol": "$$\\text{maximize net export value}$$",
    "type": "string",
    "description": "Planning objective stating that export value should be maximized while import expenditure is reduced subject to feasibility."
  }
}

Output Format
{
  "production_plan": {
    "symbol": "$$x_i$$",
    "type": "array of length $$|\\mathcal{I}|$$",
    "description": "Optimal production and export quantity for each commodity $$i \\in \\mathcal{I}$$."
  },
  "objective_value": {
    "symbol": "$$z^*$$",
    "type": "scalar",
    "description": "Optimal value of the planning objective."
  },
  "imported_input_expenditure_total": {
    "symbol": "$$m^*$$",
    "type": "scalar",
    "description": "Total imported-input expenditure implied by the optimal production plan."
  }
}

Example(s)

Input 1
{
  "commodities": ["steel", "engines", "electronic_components", "plastic"],
  "planning_horizon": ["single_period"],
  "export_prices": {
    "steel": 500,
    "engines": 1500,
    "electronic_components": 300,
    "plastic": 1200
  },
  "technical_input_coefficients": {
    "steel": {
      "engines": 0.02,
      "plastic": 0.01
    },
    "engines": {
      "steel": 0.8,
      "electronic_components": 0.15,
      "plastic": 0.11
    },
    "electronic_components": {
      "steel": 0.01,
      "engines": 0.01,
      "plastic": 0.05
    },
    "plastic": {
      "engines": 0.03,
      "steel": 0.2,
      "electronic_components": 0.05
    }
  },
  "imported_input_expenditure": {
    "steel": 250,
    "engines": 300,
    "electronic_components": 50,
    "plastic": 300
  },
  "labor_requirements": {
    "steel": {
      "value": 6,
      "unit": "person-months"
    },
    "engines": {
      "value": 1,
      "unit": "person-year"
    },
    "electronic_components": {
      "value": 6,
      "unit": "person-months"
    },
    "plastic": {
      "value": 2,
      "unit": "person-years"
    }
  },
  "capacity_upper_bounds": {
    "engines": 650000,
    "plastic": 60000
  },
  "total_labor_available": {
    "value": 830000,
    "unit": "person-months per year"
  }
}
